 "intro": "<p>One data set drawn three ways at once: a dotplot, a histogram and a boxplot. Drag any dot and every summary and every graph is recomputed from the dots you see.</p>",
 "howItWorksTitle": "How the numbers are computed",
 "howItWorks": "<p>The mean is the total divided by n. The median is the middle of the ordered values. Quartiles follow the rule AP® Statistics uses: Q1 and Q3 are the medians of the lower and upper halves, with the median itself left out when n is odd. The standard deviation is the sample SD, dividing by n − 1. A value is an outlier when it is more than 1.5 × IQR below Q1 or above Q3, and the whiskers end at the most extreme values inside those fences. Histogram bins include their left edge, so a value on an edge counts in the bin to its right.</p><p>Test yourself problems are generated from a seed: the problem code reopens the same data.</p>",
